    c1a00002: scoped, order-correct enactment delivery route (R5 prerequisite)
    
    Adds government/enactment-merge.sh and tests/enactment-merge-smoke.sh.
    
    Route properties required by the Clerk's R5 summons:
    - verifies the exact candidate commit and tree BEFORE it can land (the candidate
      is the delivery commit itself, fast-forwarded; nothing is rewritten);
    - complete path allowlist in a committed manifest, exact bijection with the
      realised delta (nothing undeclared, nothing declared-but-unchanged);
    - refuses ambiguous/absolute paths, constitution/*, government/seats.tsv, and
      any path outside records/* + government/LAWS.md;
    - refuses ballot ROW edits (records/ballots/* may only be added);
    - requires non-Clerk, non-sponsor, mutually distinct verifier and reviewer;
    - records a durable receipt bound to commit+tree+manifest+authority;
    - publish is fast-forward only, after canonical preflight; no force-push.
    
    The script grants no legal authority: it still requires Parliament to have
    enacted the authorising bill; it only refuses undeclared or unverified changes.
    
    Hermetic scope/ordering tests: 14/14 pass.

